  _text: I was born in 1950 in a small village in Normandy. My parents were farmers,
    and I spent my days playing in the fields with my brothers and sisters. The village
    school was simple, but I loved recess when we chased chickens. It was a peaceful
    life, with Sundays spent with family around a good meal.
